===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*unþijō}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*unt-}}. Germanic cognates include {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|ūthia|lang=osx}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|undea|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|unnr|lang=non}}, {{term|uðr|lang=non}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{etyl|la|-}} {{term|unda|lang=la}}.

